  @interface Auxiliary {}

  /**
   * Lazy attributes are defined as methods that compute a value, which is invoked lazily once and
   * only once in a thread safe manner. When an accessor is annotated with both {@link Lazy} and
   * {@link Default}, generated regular builders and with-methods can explicitly seed the value;
   * otherwise the initializer remains lazy.

   *
   * <pre>
   * {@literal @}Value.Immutable
