   * <p>
   * Unless also annotated with {@link Default}, this kind of attribute cannot be set during
   * building. Values are lazily computed from other attributes and stored in a non-final field,
   * while initialization is guarded by synchronization with a volatile field check. Should be
   * applied to a non-abstract method - attribute value initializer.

   * <p>
   * In general, lazy attribute initializer is more safe than using {@link Derived} attributes, lazy
   * attribute's initializer method body can refer to abstract mandatory and container attributes as
   * well as to other lazy attributes. Though lazy attributes act as {@link Auxiliary}.
